## How it all connects -- the flywheel

```
   SPEC (SPA PDF)   \
   CONFIG (.inc)     +--->  gen_manifest.py  --->  csr_manifest.csv  --+
   RTL (existent_csr)/                             + report.md         |
                                                                       |
                     safe_write_policy.csv --> gen_fixtures.py <-------+
                                                     |
                                                     v
                                            csr_survival_gen.S
                                                     |
   every suite run:                                  v
     test_registration_guard.sh ....... hash matches the build?
     test_registration_fixtures.sh .... regen + rebuild + --verify the fixture
     cold-cache hybrid --verify ....... the batched sweep = the over-claim proof
```

The compounding effect: once an engine is registered, **adding it to the test matrix is automatic** (`run_e2e.sh` takes the engine axis from the registration dirs), and every future change is re-checked by scripts, not by memory. A new config of the same core costs one `gen_manifest.py` run plus a `gen_fixtures.py` run -- the procedure, not a person, guarantees "nothing missed".

### Cheat sheet -- reproduce this engine's registration

```sh
# 1. regenerate the manifest from the three sources (needs the built vsim)
python3 tests/engines/ax45mpv_premium-ed1cb158/gen_manifest.py \
        tests/engines/ax45mpv_premium-ed1cb158

# 2. regenerate + rebuild + --verify the write-survival fixture
bash tests/engines/test_registration_fixtures.sh

# 3. the over-claim proof: a cold-cache hybrid --verify (both trigger modes)
rm -rf ~/.cache/andesim
./andesim run --mode hybrid --trigger marker --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium \
        --verify tests/fixtures/rt_c_hello.elf

# 4. the standing guards (run by scripts/test_all.sh)
bash tests/engines/test_registration_guard.sh
```

